,{"text":"position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"justify values can be different.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"halign"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"valign"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" if not specified.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"printsObject"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The justify attribute is used to indicate left, center, or right justification. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default value varies for different elements. For elements where the justify","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is present but the halign attribute is not, the justify attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates horizontal alignment as well as justification.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"justify"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to enclose the metronome mark in parentheses.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" if not specified.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"hasParentheses"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/init(id:content:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsobject:justify:hasparentheses:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/init(id:content:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:justify:hasParentheses:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Content-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Metronome."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/content-swift.enum","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome.Content","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Content-swift.enum","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLValign":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLValign","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign type is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text is on multiple lines, baseline alignment refers to the baseline of the lowest line of text. Defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are implementation-dependent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValign","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvalign","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/init(id:content:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:justify:hasParentheses:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLMetronome","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/init(id:content:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsobject:justify:hasparentheses:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"content"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV7ContentO","text":"Content"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"external